# Developed on Windows, built on Linux in CI. Three families do not survive a CRLF:
#   - mvnw: the kernel reads the shebang literally and reports "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M",
#     a message that mentions neither git nor line endings;
#   - shell scripts and container entrypoints;
#   - Flyway SQL, whose CHECKSUM is computed over the content: a CRLF would diverge from an
#     already-applied migration and Flyway would refuse to start against an existing database.
* text=auto

*.sh   text eol=lf
mvnw   text eol=lf
*.sql  text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf

mvnw.cmd text eol=crlf
